PAPER TITLE

Explainable AI–Based Detection of Pediatric Cardiovascular Diseases Using Multi-Lead ECG Signals

PROBLEM STATEMENT

Pediatric cardiovascular diseases often present subtle and age-dependent electrocardiographic patterns that are difficult to interpret consistently using conventional diagnostic approaches.

While recent advances in artificial intelligence have demonstrated promising results in ECG-based disease detection, most existing models are adult-centric and operate as black boxes, offering limited interpretability.

There is a critical need for pediatric-specific, explainable AI models that not only classify cardiovascular diseases from ECG signals but also provide clinically meaningful explanations of their decisions to support trust, validation, and adoption in pediatric healthcare settings.

